+nodes: [suite]
+brief: none
+---
+
+Move the fold's session-merge rule into `tools/fold-intervals.js`, so `trio-batch.mjs` and `cvhr-fold-rescore.mjs` import one rule.
+
+The rule is `concurrentSet` with `mergeIv`, `ivIntersect` and `ivSpan`. It decides which fragments make up a night. Before this change, `trio-batch.mjs` held the rule as module-local consts, and `cvhr-fold-rescore.mjs` kept its own copy. The fold runs its night loop at import, so no other tool could import a const from it.
+
+`tests/fold-intervals-tests.mjs` pins the known answers of the rule. It also checks that neither tool keeps its own interval loop. The `trio-batch.mjs` selftest pins the rule where the fold reads it. The selection does not change: 20000 random nights gave 0 mismatches against the old consts. This closes residue `2026-09-29-fold-session-merge-rule-is-module-local-to-trio-batch`.
