+---
+bump: patch
+type: fixed
+brief: MUTATION-SURVIVOR-LEDGER-2026-09-28-BRIEF.md
+---
+
+`tools/mutation-survivors.mjs ingest` now closes an open ledger entry when the gate run it reads excused that mutant through the equivalence ledger (`classification.excused`). The entry becomes `equivalent` and names the PR and commit of the run that excused it. A function-qualified excuse closes only that function; an unqualified one closes the text module-wide, the same rule `mutate_diff` applies. The ratchet no longer throws when the open count falls: the contract requires a PASS to carry `reason: null`, so the "lower the expected count" note moves to `result.note`.
